---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Colleen Shifflett"
  description="Ten years of analytics across financial services, SaaS, media, and government. We work on the layer of your website most teams never think about."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>
          There's the development layer, the presentation layer, and then
          there's the intelligence layer.
        </h1>

        <p>
          The development layer makes your site run. The presentation layer
          shapes what people see and experience.
        </p>
        <p>
          The intelligence layer makes it understandable, findable, measurable,
          and improvable.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's how your site is organized, what it says, how people and AI make
          sense of it, and how you learn what's working. It brings information
          design, content design, and experiment design together as one
          connected layer.
        </p>
        <p>It's a layer most teams don't see.</p>
        <p>We bring it into view.</p>

        <h2>The art, science, and math of web strategy</h2>
        <p>
          The art is the words, structure, and labels that help people see
          themselves on your site. The science is the method: small changes,
          honest feedback, and learning what works. The math is the measurement:
          data accurate enough to make decisions, without chasing perfection.
        </p>

        <h2>Where I come from</h2>
        <p>
          I've spent ten years in analytics across financial services, B2B SaaS,
          media, and federal government. I have helped launch several web
          analytics programs from small startups to large national organizations
          and businesses. I've provided training and resources for over 500
          non-technical professionals to use their own data with confidence.
          Most recently I've enhanced my experience as an embedded analytics
          engineer, keeping my technical practice sharp in alignment with my
          creative direction.
        </p>

        <h2>What I've learned</h2>
        <p>
          Right-sized beats sophisticated. The best web program is the one your
          team can actually run.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
